-- ============================================================================
-- EC1 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Cash Flow & NPV, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE FISCAL EDGES. Production sharing cost recovery
-- and the pool the rows never show, the PIA royalties by terrain and by
-- price, the hydrocarbon tax cascade with its CPR cap, its allowance and
-- its volume cap, the liquids-only HCT base and the two-thirds CIT
-- restriction, TET or the development levy by the date trigger, loss relief
-- with its separate pools, the economic limit, abandonment as a lump sum
-- and as a sinking fund, first-oil delay, and three numbers the engine
-- reports that a careful reader must distrust.
--
-- THE PIA CASCADE IS FIVE TAXES ON THREE BASES, AND THE BASE DECIDES MORE
-- THAN THE RATE, which is the shape of the tier. AKATA under the PIA
-- (shallow water, converted PML, 2029 base year so the framework is
-- nta_2025) pays royalties 122393644.64, HCT 77020493.72, CIT 86274711.53
-- and development levy 21007007.79 with no TET, NPV 42943268.01 against
-- 72534830.66 under joint venture terms. Moving the same rows to deep
-- offshore under the conservative reading zeroes the HCT and takes NPV to
-- 141623594.88; the aggressive reading gives 61725382.46. The terrain
-- string moves NPV by more than the oil price sweep from 82 to 120 does.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The rows never carry the PSC cost pool and
-- no KPI reports what is left of it at cessation; the CIT capital allowance
-- is restricted to two thirds of the assessable profit with NO carryforward
-- of what the restriction disallows (the amount on cpr_forfeiture is in the
-- extraction's FINDINGS-cashflow.md); and the
-- economic limit is off by default, so an uneconomic tail is KEPT and hands
-- the IRR a terminal negative.
--
-- THE RECORDED ENGINE DEFECT THIS TIER OWNS. The sinking-fund abandonment is
-- working-interest scaled while the lump sum is not: pia_sinking_fund_wi_50
-- collects 15000000.00 of contributions and reports total_abandonment_cost
-- 30000000.00, while jv_abandonment_wi_60 charges the full 10000000.00
-- against the 60 percent flows. Under one funding mode abandonment_cost_usd
-- is a share-level number and under the other a field-level one.
--
-- Nothing travels beyond this tier except the habit of asking, of every
-- fiscal line, which base it was charged on.
-- ============================================================================

values ('cashflow', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-cost-recovery","title":"Cost Recovery","lesson_keys":["l01-the-psc-cost-pool","l02-the-cap-binds-and-carries","l03-tranches-and-the-credit","l04-what-cost-oil-refuses"]},{"key":"m02-the-pia-royalties","title":"The PIA Royalties","lesson_keys":["l01-terrain-sets-the-rate","l02-the-marginal-blend","l03-the-price-royalty-and-its-anchors","l04-field-level-tiers-and-working-interest"]},{"key":"m03-hydrocarbon-tax","title":"Hydrocarbon Tax","lesson_keys":["l01-hcdt-and-nddc","l02-the-cost-price-ratio-cap","l03-the-allowance-and-its-volume-cap","l04-hct-on-liquids-only","l05-cit-and-the-two-thirds-restriction"]},{"key":"m04-levies-and-losses","title":"Levies and Losses","lesson_keys":["l01-tet-or-the-development-levy","l02-the-date-trigger","l03-loss-relief","l04-losses-unused-at-cessation","l05-the-minimum-effective-tax-rate"]},{"key":"m05-end-of-life","title":"End of Life","lesson_keys":["l01-the-economic-limit","l02-abandonment-as-a-lump-sum","l03-the-sinking-fund","l04-first-oil-delay","l05-three-numbers-to-distrust"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
